{"text": "Category F is Deaf or Hard of Hearing. The educational description is: A student with a medically diagnosed hearing loss that creates substantial educational difficulty. Educational planning considers language, communication, social access, and the impact of the listening environment. This description is about educational impact and the support required for meaningful participation. It should not be used as a prediction of intelligence, personality, or future potential.\n\nOur fictional student is Ethan Park, who is in Grade 9 and uses he/him pronouns. Ethan has bilateral severe hearing loss and uses cochlear implants. He communicates through spoken English and ASL, choosing the mode that best fits the setting. This background information matters because it connects the designation to observable access needs at school.\n\nWhen we plan for Ethan, we ask three practical questions: What can the student already do? What barriers are interfering with participation or learning? And what support will remove those barriers while building independence? Those questions keep the profile individualized and useful. Planning should include the student, family, teacher, case manager, and relevant specialists.\n\nI will now hand the presentation to Presenter 2, who will begin with Ethan’s strengths and communication.", "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural", "audio": "special-education-F-02.mp3", "words": [{"text": "Category", "start": 0.1, "end": 0.7, "start_char": 0, "end_char": 8}, {"text": "F", "start": 0.7125, "end": 1.025, "start_char": 9, "end_char": 10}, {"text": "is", "start": 1.0375, "end": 1.2125, "start_char": 11, "end_char": 13}, {"text": "Deaf", "start": 1.225, "end": 1.625, "start_char": 14, "end_char": 18}, {"text": "or", "start": 1.6375, "end": 1.7375, "start_char": 19, "end_char": 21}, {"text": "Hard", "start": 1.75, "end": 2.05, "start_char": 22, "end_char": 26}, {"text": "of", "start": 2.0625, "end": 2.15, "start_char": 27, "end_char": 29}, {"text": "Hearing", "